## Update third-party licenses and documentation
================================================================================

Context: Audited the ``licenses/`` inventory against dependencies in
``pyproject.toml``, ``src/mcp-server/pyproject.toml``, and client CDN assets
in ``src/front/``. Added missing licenses for newly added core/optional
dependencies and front-end sanitization libraries, added local license files,
updated pinned version constraints in the README, and synced
``docs/development.md``.

Changes:

1. licenses/python/neo4j-LICENSE.txt
   Added Apache 2.0 / PSFv2 license file for the Neo4j Python driver
   (``neo4j>=5.0`` core dependency).
2. licenses/python/psycopg-LICENSE.txt
   Added LGPL-3.0 license file for Psycopg 3 / psycopg-pool (``psycopg[binary]>=3.2.0``,
   ``psycopg-pool>=3.2.0`` optional dependency used for Lakebase registry/storage).
3. licenses/python/cryptography-LICENSE.txt
   Added Apache 2.0 / BSD 3-Clause license file for cryptography (``cryptography>=50.0.0``
   security constraint floor).
4. licenses/javascript/dompurify-LICENSE.txt
   Added Apache 2.0 / MPL 2.0 license file for DOMPurify 3.4.17 (loaded in
   ``base.html`` and used in ``utils.js`` for XSS sanitization of markdown).
5. licenses/README.md
   Added entries for DOMPurify, neo4j, psycopg, and cryptography; updated version
   floors for MLflow (>=3.17.2), Strawberry GraphQL (>=0.327.2), FastMCP (>=3.4.10),
   and Marked (15.0.12); updated License Summary table with LGPL-3.0 and additions.
6. docs/development.md
   Updated dependency reference tables: added neo4j, DOMPurify, and Marked; updated
   version numbers for MLflow, FastMCP, and black.

